pages.content_en:
For the theory test, you should recognise the type of sign and understand its meaning.

The signs covered here include:

- dangerous bend to the right;
- dangerous bend to the left;
- successive bends with the first bend to the left;
- successive bends with the first bend to the right;
- dangerous descent;
- steep ascent;
- falling rocks;
- loose chippings;
- road narrows;
- road narrows on the left;
- road narrows on the right;
- uneven road or hump;
- raised traffic-calming feature;
- opening bridge;
- road leading onto a quay or riverbank;
- slippery road;
- slippery road due to snow or ice;
- roadworks;
- low-flying aircraft;
- side winds;
- cattle crossing;
- wild animals;
- general danger;
- railway or tram tracks crossing the road;
- traffic queue;
- dead-end road;
- dead-end road except for cyclists and pedestrians;
- N-road.

A warning sign is normally placed before the danger.

An additional plate may indicate that the danger begins at a different distance or continues over a stated distance.

